menu "busware USB reset guard"

    config BUSWARE_USB_RESET_GUARD
        bool "Restart once by software after a reset over the USB-Serial-JTAG port"
        depends on SOC_USB_SERIAL_JTAG_SUPPORTED
        default y if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6
        default n
        help
            A reset over the USB-Serial-JTAG port (a terminal or flasher
            toggling DTR/RTS) is a core reset that does not reset the modem
            subsystem.  On the ESP32-C6 the Wi-Fi station afterwards found no
            access point in about 8 % of such resets until the next restart.
            With this option busware_usb_reset_guard(), called first in
            app_main(), restarts the chip once by software after such a
            reset (not while an OTA image awaits confirmation).  On by
            default on the ESP32-C6, where it was measured.

endmenu
